<.shell title="Forms" current={:forms}>
  <h1>Forms</h1>
  <p class="lead">
    Bold labels above, hints under them, errors on the field.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>Label md semibold. Hint sm muted. Error md bold in <code>--danger</code>. Input md.</li>
    <li>
      Inputs are 40px tall with a 2px border. Small inputs (32px, sm text) are for filter bars only.
    </li>
    <li>Fields are 24px apart. Width follows the expected answer, not the page.</li>
    <li>
      A form with a save button uses checkboxes, never switches. A switch is for a setting that takes effect when it's tapped.
    </li>
    <li>
      In the app: <code>&lt;.input field=&#123;@form[:name]&#125; label="Full name"&gt;</code>, with the hint as its inner block.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Elements</h2>

  <h3>Text input</h3>
  <div class="demo">
    <.input id="e-name" name="e-name" label="Full name" value="Avery Chen" />
    <div class="max-w-80">
      <.input id="e-email" name="e-email" type="email" label="Email" value="avery@example.com">
        SAR Duty sends the tax credit letter here.
      </.input>
    </div>
    <div class="max-w-40">
      <.input id="e-ref" name="e-ref" label="Member ID" value="101" />
    </div>
  </div>
  <p class="spec">
    Three widths: full, medium (<code>max-w-80</code>, 320px), and small (<code>max-w-40</code>, 160px).
  </p>

  <h3>Select, date, and text area</h3>
  <div class="demo">
    <div class="max-w-80">
      <.input
        id="e-kind"
        name="e-kind"
        type="select"
        label="Activity kind"
        options={["Incident", "Exercise", "Event"]}
        value="Incident"
      />
      <.input id="e-date" name="e-date" type="date" label="Start date" value="2025-09-28" />
    </div>
    <.input
      id="e-notes"
      name="e-notes"
      type="textarea"
      label="Notes"
      rows="3"
      value="Subject found at 21:10, walked out with the team."
    />
  </div>

  <h3>Checkboxes</h3>
  <div class="demo">
    <.input
      id="e-refresh"
      name="e-refresh"
      type="checkbox"
      label="Refresh from D4H every night"
      checked
    >
      SAR Duty refreshes at 02:00.
    </.input>
    <fieldset class="mb-p">
      <legend class="font-semibold">Activities to include</legend>
      <.hint>Meetings and public events count as events.</.hint>
      <label class="flex items-center gap-2 my-1"><input type="checkbox" checked /> Incidents</label>
      <label class="flex items-center gap-2 my-1"><input type="checkbox" checked /> Exercises</label>
      <label class="flex items-center gap-2 my-1"><input type="checkbox" /> Events</label>
    </fieldset>
  </div>
  <p class="spec">
    24px boxes. One setting is an <code>&lt;.input type="checkbox"&gt;</code>. Several that answer one question sit in a fieldset whose legend is the question, as on the organization page.
  </p>

  <h3>Radios</h3>
  <div class="demo">
    <fieldset class="mb-p">
      <legend class="font-semibold">Hours to count</legend>
      <label class="flex items-center gap-2 my-1">
        <input type="radio" name="e-hours" checked /> Primary and secondary
      </label>
      <label class="flex items-center gap-2 my-1">
        <input type="radio" name="e-hours" /> Primary only
      </label>
    </fieldset>
  </div>
  <p class="spec not-yet">Not used in the app yet. They take the checkbox list's markup.</p>

  <h3>Switches</h3>
  <div class="demo">
    <div class="max-w-100 space-y-4">
      <.switch id="e-sound" label="Sound" checked>A tone for each scan.</.switch>
      <.switch id="e-off" label="Off" />
      <.switch id="e-disabled" label="Disabled" checked disabled />
      <.switch id="e-focus" label="Keyboard focus" class="is-focus" />
    </div>
  </div>
  <p class="spec">
    A switch changes a setting the moment it's tapped. Label on the leading edge, switch on the trailing edge, a 48 by 28px track. Inside a form with a save button, use a checkbox: a switch says the change already happened. In the app: <code>&lt;.switch id="…" label="…"&gt;</code>.
  </p>

  <h3>Compact switch</h3>
  <div class="demo">
    <div class="max-w-100">
      <.button variant={:success} class="w-full">Scan ID cards</.button>
      <.switch id="e-compact" label="Sound" compact checked class="mt-2" />
    </div>
  </div>
  <p class="spec">
    One page-level setting under the page's main action, such as Sound under the scan button. A small muted label and the switch, together on the trailing edge. No hint. The track stays full size, since it's tapped in a hurry. In the app: <code>&lt;.switch … compact&gt;</code>.
  </p>

  <h3>Read-only, disabled, and error</h3>
  <div class="demo">
    <div class="max-w-80">
      <.input id="e-ro" name="e-ro" label="Latitude" value="49.7553" readonly>
        From D4H. Change it there.
      </.input>
      <.input id="e-dis" name="e-dis" label="Region" value="Canada" disabled />
      <.input
        id="e-err"
        name="e-err"
        label="Yard coordinate"
        value="49.7553 -123.131"
        errors={["Enter latitude and longitude separated by a comma"]}
      >
        Latitude and longitude, like 49.75533, -123.13110.
      </.input>
    </div>
  </div>
  <p class="spec">
    A field shows its error only after the person has typed in it or tried to save.
  </p>

  <h2>Team settings, with errors</h2>
  <div class="example max-w-160">
    <div class="error-summary" role="alert">
      <h2>There is a problem</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><a href="#authorized_by">Enter who authorizes tax letters</a></li>
        <li><a href="#d4h_key">The D4H access key was not accepted by D4H</a></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <.input id="name" name="name" label="Team name" value="Squamish SAR" />
    <div class="grid grid-cols-2 gap-x-5">
      <.input id="lat" name="lat" label="Latitude" value="49.7553" readonly />
      <.input id="lng" name="lng" label="Longitude" value="-123.1311" readonly />
    </div>
    <div class="max-w-80">
      <.input
        id="tz"
        name="tz"
        type="select"
        label="Time zone"
        options={["America/Vancouver", "America/Edmonton"]}
        value="America/Vancouver"
      />
    </div>
    <.input
      id="address"
      name="address"
      type="textarea"
      label="Mailing address"
      rows="3"
      value={Enum.join(["PO Box 123", "Squamish BC V8B 0A1"], "\n")}
    />
    <.input
      id="authorized_by"
      name="authorized_by"
      type="textarea"
      label="Tax letters authorized by"
      rows="3"
      value=""
      errors={["Enter who authorizes tax letters"]}
    >
      Full name, title, address, and phone of the president or a similar role. CRA uses it in audits.
    </.input>
    <.input
      id="d4h_key"
      name="d4h_key"
      type="password"
      label="D4H access key"
      value="not-a-real-key"
      errors={["The D4H access key was not accepted by D4H"]}
    >
      One key for every D4H request. Stored encrypted.
    </.input>
    <.form_actions>
      <.button variant={:primary}>Save settings</.button>
      <.button>Refresh from D4H</.button>
    </.form_actions>
  </div>
  <p class="spec not-yet">
    The error summary is not used in the app yet. See <a href={page_path(:feedback)}>Messages</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Group qualification rules</h2>
  <p>An inline editor: small inputs and small buttons, since it sits inside a page.</p>
  <div class="example">
    <div :for={clause <- clauses()} class="mb-p border rounded px-p py-p05">
      <div class="flex flex-wrap md:flex-nowrap justify-between items-center gap-2 mb-p05">
        <div class="flex flex-wrap md:flex-nowrap items-center gap-2">
          <input
            type="text"
            value={clause.name}
            placeholder="Name, for example First Aid"
            aria-label="Clause name"
            class="rounded border shadow-sm text-sm font-semibold"
          />
          <h3 class="font-semibold">— member must hold any of:</h3>
        </div>
        <.button variant={:danger} size={:sm}>Delete clause</.button>
      </div>
      <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-2 mb-p05">
        <span
          :for={q <- clause.qualifications}
          class={[
            "inline-flex items-center gap-2 rounded px-2 py-1 text-sm",
            if(String.starts_with?(q, "Missing"),
              do: "border border-danger-1 text-danger-1",
              else: "bg-base-2"
            )
          ]}
        >
          {q}
          <button class="text-danger-1 hover:text-danger-2 font-bold" title="Remove qualification">
            &times;
          </button>
        </span>
        <span :if={clause.qualifications == []} class="text-secondary-1 text-sm italic">
          No qualifications yet
        </span>
      </div>
      <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-2 items-end">
        <select class="block rounded border shadow-sm text-sm max-w-xs truncate">
          <option value="">Select a qualification</option>
          <option>Rope Rescue Technician</option>
          <option>Swiftwater Rescue</option>
        </select>
        <.button size={:sm}>Add qualification</.button>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-2">
      <.button size={:sm}>Add clause</.button>
      <.button variant={:primary} size={:sm}>Done</.button>
    </div>
  </div>
  <p class="spec">
    The markup of the clause editor in <code>Web.GroupLive</code>, with made-up clauses.
  </p>

  <h2>Import attendance</h2>
  <div class="example max-w-160">
    <.input id="import" name="import" type="textarea" label="Attendance report" rows="8" value="">
      Paste the report exported by SAR Assist. Members are matched by name, email, or phone.
      You review every change before it's made.
    </.input>
    <.button variant={:primary}>Import attendance</.button>
  </div>
</.shell>
